WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870
- How did you come up

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.390
with the title of your
book, "Mixed Plate,"

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:03.310
How did you come up with that?

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:06.750
- Uh Mixed Plate, it's just like, okay.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.430
One, I'm in love with Hawaii.
- Yeah.

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.230
- You know what I mean? Hawaii
really embraced me right away

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:14.452
when my first special came out,
I broke a record in Hawaii.

00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:15.490
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.310
- I got like my own day in Hawaii.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.070
I sold like 27,000 tickets

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.920
at this theater called
the Blaisdell theater.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.990
I broke Mariah Carey's record.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:23.823
- What?
- Yeah.

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:25.400
It was like the most tickets ever sold,

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.830
and I gave it my own day.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.510
And I just love the culture there.

00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:30.020
I love the people there.

00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.280
And one of the things I love, you know,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.610
to eat was the mixed plate.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.510
And when you look at the
mixed plate it has everything.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.362
Like every ethnicity is on the plate.

00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:39.195
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:39.195 --> 00:00:40.900
- There's a little rice for Asians,

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.480
there's Korean barbecue,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.864
there's tempura, Japanese,

00:00:43.864 --> 00:00:45.520
there's spam on it,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.960
there's mac salad.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.870
So when you look at that
plate, I think of me.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.630
It's like a little bit
of all these cultures

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.690
just mixed up into me.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.350
And I just felt like that's
a good representation

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:59.430
of what this book is and
about my life in this world.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.000
- That's a beautiful way
to look at the world.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.737
- Yeah, 'cause you put all
that stuff on one plate

00:01:03.737 --> 00:01:06.930
and it just becomes this
beautiful plate of food.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.030
You know what I mean?
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.597
- And I feel like that's
what it took to make-

00:01:09.597 --> 00:01:10.600
- But I just mean, it's society.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.545
- It's cool-
- - [Jo Koy] Yeah.

00:01:11.545 --> 00:01:12.500
- to look at the world like that.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.370
- [Jo Koy] Yeah.
- Like we all count,

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:14.203
we all matter,

00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:15.390
we all make the plate beautiful.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.420
- Yeah, you put it all-
- Even spam.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.527
Even redneck spam.
- Even spam.

00:01:19.628 --> 00:01:20.810
Put spam next to a filet mignon.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:21.800
You know what?

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.950
I'm eating that spam.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.280
- Fine, it's fancier.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.600
Tastes better already.

